#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_e3

#% text
# `weierstrass_e3([g2, g3])` gives the root `e3 = weierstrass_p(omega3, [g2, g3])` of `4 t^3 - g2 t - g3`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The half-periods `omega_k` are those of `weierstrass_half_periods` (`omega2 = -omega1 - omega3`).

#% item
# The three roots add up to zero; for `[a, 0]` with `a > 0` and `[0, b]` with `b > 0` the values are closed forms.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_e3([11.0, 7.0])
#% output
#= -1.0

#% cell
n(weierstrass_e3([5, 1]), 25)
#% output
#= -1.0000000000000000000000000000

#% cell
weierstrass_e3([0.5 + im, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.6985557102983584 + 0.13215450229530867im

#% cell
weierstrass_e3([1, 0])
#% output
#= -1/2

#% text
# The roots add up to zero:

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e2([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e3([5.0, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.0

